# ResearchSpec Mixed-License Notice

ResearchSpec is distributed under multiple licenses. A single SPDX identifier would not accurately describe the complete package.

## MIT-licensed material

Unless identified below as ARSU-derived material, ResearchSpec-authored source code, tests, documentation, Companion Skills, and command adapters are licensed under the MIT License, copyright 2026 ResearchSpec contributors. The complete text is in `LICENSES/MIT.txt`.

The standalone paper–patent comparison Procedure is original ResearchSpec MIT
material. The eighteen vendor-derived fixed patent capabilities adapt MIT
material by handsomestWei, copyright 2026, and include the upstream license.
Bundled Mermaid and Three.js resources retain their own MIT notices. The seven
patent and research/patent composition profiles are ResearchSpec-authored MIT
graph declarations; licenses of referenced academic packages remain unchanged.

Joshua Reed's (`leike0813`) original Chinese Patent Helper material is licensed
under the MIT License with the owner's explicit authorization, including the
source content under `vendor/chinese-patent-helper/upstream/**` and
`authoring/chinese-patent-helper/**`. The published Procedure under
`skills/capabilities/generation-chinese-patent-filing/**` retains the source
copyright and complete MIT text. The official template and CC0 profile
identified below retain their stated origins.

## CC BY-NC 4.0 material

The following material is adapted from Academic Research Skills (ARS), copyright 2026 Cheng-I Wu, and remains licensed under the Creative Commons Attribution-NonCommercial 4.0 International License:

- `vendor/ars/**`
- `skills/arsu/**`, except the seven MIT graph declarations
  `patent-disclosure`, `patent-application`, `patent-docket`, `patent-intelligence`,
  `patent-oa`, `research-to-patent` and `patent-informed-paper` under `profiles/`
- `src/arsu-converter/routing/catalog.ts`
- `src/arsu-converter/workflow/catalog.ts`
- `src/core/workflow/profiles/arsu-v0-1.generated.ts`
- their compiled equivalents under `dist/**`

The canonical license identifier and URL are recorded in `LICENSES/CC-BY-NC-4.0.txt`. Complete copies of the upstream license are included as `LICENSE` inside every packaged ARSU Skill directory.

The MIT grant does not remove or override the noncommercial restriction on ARSU-derived material. Commercial distribution or use of the combined package may require separate permission from the relevant rights holder. This file documents the project's engineering interpretation and is not legal advice.

## AGPL-3.0-only material

The fixed Zotero literature Adapter under `literature-adapters/zotero/**` is
derived from the pinned Zotero Agents source and bundle release recorded in its
`NOTICE.md` and `DERIVATION.json` files. It is distributed under GNU Affero
General Public License version 3 only. The complete license text is available at
`LICENSES/AGPL-3.0.txt` and is copied into each generated Adapter Skill.

The AGPL-3.0-only terms apply to the identified Adapter material and do not
replace the licenses of ResearchSpec-authored, ARSU-derived, or domain Skill
material.

## Apache-2.0 material

Generated FinRobot-derived Skills under `skills/plugins/vendors/finrobot/**`
and independently reimplemented HistAgent-derived Skills under
`skills/plugins/vendors/histagent/**` are distributed under Apache License 2.0
after source, origin, license, and derivation review. Each Skill contains its
complete `LICENSE`, attribution `NOTICE`, source revision, and derivation
manifest. A reference copy of the license is available at
`LICENSES/Apache-2.0.txt`.

The Apache-2.0 grant applies only to the reviewed FinRobot- and HistAgent-derived material
identified by those files and does not change the licenses of ARSU-derived,
ResearchSpec-authored, or other vendor material.

